From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seilent <github@seilent.net>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:19:06 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: Invert the battery current on
 the Lenovo Legion Y700 2025

The battery manager firmware on the Lenovo Legion Y700 2025 reports the
battery current inverted: -7.58 A while it charges from a PD charger and
+0.85 A while it discharges. The power supply ABI has charging current
positive, and UPower takes a negative current_now as discharging, so the
battery shows as discharging while it charges.

Invert the battery current on this board.

Signed-off-by: seilent <github@seilent.net>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index 58e238e6f..3e9ffca2b 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
 #include <linux/nvmem-consumer.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/of_device.h>
 #include <linux/power_supply.h>
 #include <linux/property.h>
@@ -325,6 +326,7 @@ struct qcom_battmgr {
 	struct completion ack;
 
 	bool service_up;
+	bool invert_current;
 
 	struct qcom_battmgr_info info;
 	struct qcom_battmgr_status status;
@@ -1461,6 +1463,8 @@ static void qcom_battmgr_sm8350_callback(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr,
 			break;
 		case BATT_CURR_NOW:
 			battmgr->status.current_now = le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.value);
+			if (battmgr->invert_current)
+				battmgr->status.current_now = -battmgr->status.current_now;
 			break;
 		case BATT_TEMP:
 			val = le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.value);
@@ -1685,6 +1689,8 @@ static int qcom_battmgr_probe(struct auxiliary_device *adev,
 	else
 		battmgr->variant = QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8350;
 
+	battmgr->invert_current = of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,tb321fu");
+
 	ret = qcom_battmgr_charge_control_thresholds_init(battmgr);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
-- 
